<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI23-IMPORTANT-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI23-IMPORTANT-002" ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T06:25:35Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S3 ;
  triage:title "Peer HTTPS listener spawns unbounded per-connection threads with no concurrency cap or handle reaping" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs accept_loop (around line 339-402) spawns a new OS thread per accepted TCP connection via spawn_request_worker with no concurrency limit, unlike the local loopback listener in the same crate (local_tcp_transport.rs) which enforces MAX_CONCURRENT_CONNECTIONS = 64. Resulting JoinHandles accumulate in HttpsListenerSet.requests: Arc<Mutex<Vec<JoinHandle<()>>>> and are only drained at full listener shutdown -- nothing reaps completed handles during normal uptime. This listener is untrusted-by-default per ADR-034 (peer authentication happens inside the spawned worker, after accept), so a remote peer can open connections faster than they complete, growing live thread count and the tracking Vec unboundedly for the life of the process." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:category "RSH" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-24T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T22:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Independently re-verified against PR #642 real current head 4315ad0a (not accepted from arch-ctm self-report). Root cause of the ubuntu-latest CI regression documented in the prior closureNote (accept_loop treating shutdown's own local wake-up connection as real peer work, consuming the bounded shutdown join window) was fixed at 569ccb47: accept_loop now calls peer_connection_admission(stop, active_connections) and takes PeerConnectionAdmission::Stop before ever spawning a worker for a post-shutdown accept -- read the diff directly, this is a real production-code change, not a test-only suppression. 4315ad0a then removed the two real-socket/wall-clock tests that were flaky on ubuntu-latest (shutdown_bounds_an_incomplete_peer_handshake, shutdown_joins_an_incomplete_peer_request_within_its_deadline) and replaced them with peer_connection_admission_is_deterministic_for_shutdown_and_capacity, a pure unit test asserting the Stop/CapacityExceeded/Admit decision table exhaustively. This directly and deterministically covers the mechanism that caused the regression. NOTED GAP (not blocking): no remaining test asserts, via a real socket and wall-clock, that HttpsListenerSet::shutdown() actually joins a genuinely incomplete external connection within its deadline end-to-end -- that integration-level timing assertion was dropped along with the flaky tests, and only the pure admission-decision logic is now covered. gh pr checks 642 at real head 4315ad0a: 8/8 legs pass (verified directly, not from any prior claim)." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-002/AI23/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-002/AI24/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-002/AI26/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-002/s27/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-002/s27-fixed-5a528661> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-002/s27-fixed-4315ad0a> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s27/4315ad0a> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s27/4315ad0a> .

